# Reject Candidate Dialog

A modal that asks for **why** before a candidate is rejected: a reason from the Rejection Reason vocabulary, plus an optional free-text note. Confirming hands both to the caller, which runs Reject Candidate.

```hbs
<RejectCandidateDialog
  @isOpen={{this.rejecting}}
  @candidateName={{this.candidate.name}}
  @onConfirm={{this.reject}}
  @onCancel={{this.closeReject}}
/>
```

```ts
import { RejectCandidateDialog } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/hr/components/reject-candidate-dialog';
```

The reason is a choice, not free text, so rejections can be counted by cause; the note carries what the choice can't. The dialog holds no state between openings and writes nothing itself: the caller owns the command run.

### Non-goals

Does not notify the candidate. Does not run the rejection.
